[Open the public Overleaf]([REDACTED PRIVATE OVERLEAF URL]

Yes—roughly one focused release pass away. The core package already exists: annotated edition, clean transcription, full verification workbench, five-page mathematical overview, literature, exact-check ledgers, scripts, and compiled QA’d PDFs.

Before minting a defensible Zenodo DOI, I still need to:

- freeze the current mathematical status and propagate the last results;
- turn the overview plus workbench into one coherent primary monograph;
- exclude raw/private session material and generate curated provenance;
- finalize attribution, license, metadata, bibliography, manifests, and checksums;
- rebuild, visually verify, round-trip the release ZIP, synchronize Overleaf, then upload and verify the public Zenodo record.

I’d call it about 85% ready. A good strategy is to publish a clearly numbered first release soon, with genuinely open items labelled open, then issue later Zenodo versions if further verification changes anything.

Also, this task’s 2,071 completed sub-agent rollouts—3.058 GB—are now archived, hash-verified, and deleted from the live session tree. The active root record was preserved.
